&gt; If I summon a desktop on screen 1 and it&#x27;s currently displayed on screen 2, they should swap.<p>At least i3&#x27;s (and I imagine sway&#x27;s) config is sufficiently flexible for that. Here&#x27;s a shell function that brings the workspace you specify to your current output:<p><pre><code>  i3_bring_workspace_to_focused_output() {
    local workspace=&quot;$1&quot;
    i3 &quot;
      workspace $workspace 
      move workspace to output $(
        i3-msg -t get_workspaces |
        jq -r &#x27;.[]|select(.focused).output&#x27;
      )
    &quot;
  }
</code></pre>
You can turn that into an executable and have it be called through a keybinding.
